# Attachments are payroll justifications - scanned memoranda, medical
# certificates - uploaded through the Coverage & Attachments screen. See
# app/Attachments.php's own header: "a guessable URL under public/ would
# serve them to anyone who asked."
#
# That comment assumes this directory sits outside the web root, which is
# true for a normal deployment and FALSE for shared hosting (InfinityFree and
# similar), where everything must live under htdocs/ and this file is the
# only thing standing between the internet and every document in it.
#
# There is deliberately no authenticated download path to replace this with -
# apiGetAttachment returns metadata only, and no download.php-style endpoint
# reads the file bytes back (see the Backlog and RouteTableTest's own note on
# apiGetAttachment). Until one exists, this .htaccess is the entire
# protection an uploaded file has.

<IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
    Require all denied
</IfModule>
<IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
    Order allow,deny
    Deny from all
</IfModule>

Options -Indexes
